&#x000a0;&#x000b1;&#x000a0;7.76<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn1">*</xref><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn2">#</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">FS</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">27.39&#x000a0;&#x000b1;&#x000a0;3.19</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">27.18&#x000a0;&#x000b1;&#x000a0;4.67</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.16&#x000a0;&#x000b1;&#x000a0;4.08</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">16.31&#x000a0;&#x000b1;&#x000a0;5.27<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn1">*</xref><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn2">#</xref></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Results shown are mean&#x000a0;&#x000b1;&#x000a0;S.D. E: peak early transmitral filling velocity during early diastole; A: peak transmitral atrial filling velocity during late diastole; Eat: acceleration time of E-wave; Edt: deceleration time of E-wave; EF: ejection fraction; FS: fractional shortening.</p></fn><fn id="tblfn1"><label>*</label><p><italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05 compared to 1st week data.</p></fn><fn id="tblfn2"><label>#</label><p><italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05 compared to normal rats.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>